FastAPI 
  is a modern, high-speed Python web framework used to build APIs (Application Programming Interfaces) that let different software applications talk to each other
Advntages:
  Super Fast Speed
  Automatic Documentation->automatically creates interactive web pages (Swagger UI) where you can see and test your API endpoints
  Automatic Data Validation-> It checks incoming data using Python type hints. If a user sends text instead of a number, FastAPI blocks the request immediately and explains the error, saving you from writing manual check code
  Less Code, Fewer Bugs
  Asynchronous Support-> It handles many requests at the same time without waiting for slow tasks (like database lookups) to finish first,keeping the app smooth and responsive
JSON (JavaScript Object Notation)
  is a lightweight text format used for storing and transporting data. 
  In Python, JSON is handled through a built-in library called the json module, meaning you do not need to install any external packages to use it.
  While a JSON object looks almost identical to a Python dictionary, they are fundamentally different: 
  JSON is always a string format, whereas a Python dictionary is an in-memory data structure
Advantages of api
  Code Reusability:Developers do not need to "reinvent the wheel" for standard features. Instead of writing complex components from scratch, they can integrate pre-built APIs for services like Google Maps geolocation, payments, or identity authentication.
  Faster Development Cycles
  Language Independence:APIs enable software systems built in completely different programming languages (like Python, Java, or Ruby) to connect effortlessly using lightweight formats like JSON
  Stability via Versioning: Well-designed APIs use versioning controls (e.g., v2 or v3 tags in the URL). This permits updates and new features to launch without breaking existing application code

